      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To improve granularity in high-variance urban ZIP codes, consider measuring community-level indicators like unemployment rates, education levels within 0.5 miles, and the prevalence of single-family homes versus multi-unit dwellings. These sociodemographic factors often serve as strong proxies for creditworthiness and property stability that raw financial data misses. Incorporating GIS-based metrics such as distance to public transit, crime indices, and recent gentrification trends can further refine your localized risk profiles.",
