      "content": "those are good starting points, definitely standard. but what i'm really after are the deeper variables that might not be in a standard census report. like, if we're trying to get really hyper-local with the risk profiles, are there any specific community makeup or cultural markers that correlate with higher claim frequency or lower policy retention? just trying to see if there are non-obvious social patterns we're missing.",
